alarm|warning-device|NOUN|device or sound giving a warning|A device or sound that warns people about danger or a situation needing attention.|chuông báo động; thiết bị báo hiệu|The alarm sounded when smoke reached the kitchen sensor.|Chuông báo động reo khi khói tới cảm biến trong bếp.|Countable; set off an alarm means cause it to give a warning.|0
alarm|cause-worry|VERB|make someone worried or afraid|To make someone feel worried or afraid about what may happen.|làm lo ngại; làm hoảng sợ|The sudden drop in water pressure alarmed the caretaker.|Áp lực nước giảm đột ngột khiến người quản lý tòa nhà lo ngại.|Transitive alarm someone; the cause is the subject and the worried person is the object.|1
alarm|fear|NOUN|worry caused by possible danger|A feeling of worry or fear when something seems dangerous or wrong.|sự lo sợ; sự hoảng hốt|She watched with alarm as the branch bent over the road.|Cô ấy lo sợ nhìn cành cây cong xuống phía trên con đường.|Usually uncountable in with alarm or cause alarm; distinct from a warning device.|2
forth|and-more|ADVERB|continuing an unfinished list|Used in and so forth to suggest more items of the kind already mentioned.|vân vân; và những thứ tương tự|Bring pencils, paper, glue, and so forth for the craft session.|Hãy mang bút chì, giấy, keo dán, vân vân cho buổi làm đồ thủ công.|This sense occurs in the phrase and so forth after a list; forth alone does not mean et cetera.|0
forth|outward|ADVERB|out or forwards from a place|Out from a place or forwards from a starting point.|ra; về phía trước|Music came forth from the open doorway.|Tiếng nhạc vọng ra từ ô cửa đang mở.|Formal or literary after movement or emergence verbs; back and forth describes repeated movement in opposite directions.|1
increase|become-more|VERB|become or make greater|To become greater in amount, size, or number, or make something greater.|tăng; làm tăng|The library increased its opening hours during the exam period.|Thư viện tăng giờ mở cửa trong kỳ thi.|Transitive increase something or intransitive something increases; increase by gives the change and increase to gives the new level.|0
increase|growth|NOUN|rise in amount or size|A rise in the amount, size, or number of something.|sự tăng lên; mức tăng|There was an increase in visitors after the exhibition opened.|Số khách tăng lên sau khi triển lãm mở cửa.|Countable in an increase in something; by/to distinguish the amount of change from the resulting level.|1
return|go-back|VERB|go back to an earlier place|To go back to a place where you were before.|trở về; quay lại|We returned to the village before the evening rain.|Chúng tôi trở về làng trước cơn mưa chiều.|Intransitive return to a place; return home has no to before home.|0
return|coming-back|NOUN|act of coming back|The act of coming back to a place or situation.|sự trở về; lần quay lại|Her return to the choir pleased the other singers.|Việc cô ấy trở lại dàn hợp xướng khiến các ca sĩ khác vui mừng.|Usually a return to something; possessive forms such as her return identify who comes back.|1
return|give-back|VERB|give something back|To give or send something back to its owner or an earlier place.|trả lại; gửi lại|Please return the borrowed tools to the shed.|Hãy trả những dụng cụ đã mượn về nhà kho.|Transitive return something to someone or somewhere; the object is what is given back.|2
trace|follow-evidence|VERB|find by following signs|To find a person, thing, or origin by following available signs or evidence.|truy tìm; lần theo dấu vết|They traced the missing parcel to a neighbouring shop.|Họ lần theo dấu vết và tìm được bưu kiện thất lạc ở cửa hàng bên cạnh.|Transitive trace something to a place or source; the endpoint is introduced by to.|0
trace|remaining-sign|NOUN|small sign that something was present|A sign left by something that was present or happened earlier.|dấu vết|The muddy floor showed traces of the visitors' boots.|Sàn nhà lấm bùn có dấu vết giày của các vị khách.|Countable; traces of something are signs of its earlier presence.|1
trace|tiny-amount|NOUN|very small amount|A very small amount of a substance or quality.|lượng rất nhỏ; chút ít|There was a trace of paint on his sleeve.|Có một vệt sơn rất nhỏ trên tay áo của anh ấy.|Countable in a trace of; emphasizes a small amount rather than a complete absence.|2
trace|copy-outline|VERB|copy by following an outline|To copy a drawing by following its lines through or on another surface.|đồ lại; can theo nét|She traced the leaf shape onto thin paper.|Cô ấy đồ lại hình chiếc lá lên giấy mỏng.|Transitive trace a shape onto a surface; distinct from finding something through evidence.|3
